  "Number": 9,
  "Question": "The value of \\(x-y^{x-y}\\) when \\(x=2\\) and \\(y=-2\\) is:",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(-18\\)",
    "B": "\\(-14\\)",
    "C": "\\(14\\)",
    "D": "\\(18\\)",
    "E": "\\(256\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "B",
  "Solution": "The value \\(-2\\) replaces the entire base \\(y\\), so put it in parentheses. First evaluate the exponent:\n\\[\nx-y=2-(-2)=4.\n\\]\nThen compute the power before the outside subtraction:\n\\[\nx-y^{x-y}\n=2-(-2)^4\n=2-16\n=-14.\n\\]\nThe fourth power is positive because it contains four negative factors. The answer is \\(-14\\), choice \\(\\mathrm{B}\\).",
